<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30122" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγκαρπ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>containing fruit</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλυξιν ἐγκάρποις χθονός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					25
				</span></i>
			; <i>fruitful</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπέρματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					276b
				</span></i>
			; of soil, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				2.4.2
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γᾶν ἔγκαρπον φέρειν</span> may
			the earth bear <i>produce</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				526.41
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Crete</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δένδρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.2e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέλη ἔγκαρπα</span> tithe <i>of
				produce</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				238
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρήσιμον καὶ ἔ.</span>
			<i>fruitful</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.776b
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Merc.Cond.</u>
				39
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			). Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πως</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, διακεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aen.Tact.
					7.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγκαρπα, τά</span>, <i>festoons of fruit</i> on friezes or the
			capitals of columns, Lat. <i>encarpa</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Vitr.
				4.1.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγκαρπα</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγκαρτα,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς κεκουρευμένους
				πυρούς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
			</span></i> Trag.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i> (ap.<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
